    "1. OVERLAY EFFICACY IS IN-SAMPLE: VB's MDD benefit derives from the 2021 episode (in-sample for threshold choice, ledger flag #4). OOS 2022-26 VB is net cost: CAGR -1.3pp/yr, Sharpe -0.03, MDD -1.3pp worse; paired OOS bootstrap p(dCAGR<=0)=0.96, p(dMDD<=0)=0.81.",
    "2. FULL-sample paired bootstrap: dMDD median +6.0pp but p(dMDD<=0)=0.283 (not significant); dCAGR p=0.46. The overlay's improvement is economically large, statistically unresolved.",
    "3. SHIPPED MDD -42.5% (stamp-exact FULL) exceeds strategist projection -40%; sits inside user tolerance 40-50% but with reduced margin. One verified crash-cascade 5-min fill (2021-05-13, -504bp vs decision close) accounts for ~3.6pp of trough depth vs parity accounting.",
    "4. SELECTION-RULE WINDOW AMBIGUITY: verdict hinges on reading criterion (i) on FULL (A1 ships) vs OOS (A0 ships). My reading: FULL (rule qualifies OOS explicitly for (ii)/(iii) only; bootstrap defined per arm x window in spec 13.4; tail insurance is only measurable where tails exist).",
    "5. OOS point estimates vs target: shipped OOS CAGR 20.5% (>=15% target met), but 2024-26 sub-window CAGR 12.4% < 15%; OOS Sharpe 0.723. Honest forward ~15-20%/yr is achievable only if 2023-type trend years recur; 2022-type years earn 0 (flat).",
    "6. Parameter surface is not flat in P&L terms (k=10 > k=5 everywhere; X>=110 useless) - the shipped (100,5) is mid-pack, not optimal; do not re-optimize (frozen), but size for model risk.",
    "7. Statistical fragility inherited from QR: gate edge vs no-gate p~0.14-0.25; DSR(A0)=0.883, DSR(A1)=0.870 (N=30 trials) - below the 0.95 bar; evidence base ~2 bears.",
    "8. Funding regime: 2021 in-market funding bleed -41.8% of start-of-year equity (A0) / -24.8% (A1); 2026 only -1.25%. A 2021-repeat compresses in-market CAGR toward zero; monitoring KPI per spec 14.",
    "9. A1 vs A0 cost of insurance OOS: -1.3pp/yr CAGR + 2.6% extra blocked gate-on days; premium is dead cost in no-crisis regimes by construction.",
    "10. Worst held day A1 = -12.68% (2021-05-12, breaker reacts next execution only); unconditional BTC worst day -40% (2020-03-12, flat) is the honest tail for any 1x long; no daily-close overlay reacts faster than the print."
